%%abcts shapes neither corpus writes, swept through both engines one at a time. Two of
%%abcts these are rules; four are open rows, measured through abcjs 6.7.0 and NOT built:
%%abcts   X:4  !trill!z4     a decoration on a REST reserves less here — page 135.368
%%abcts                      against abcjs's 147.1135, 11.75px.
%%abcts   X:5  {g}z2         a grace group on a REST: abcjs shifts the whole line 10px
%%abcts                      right and draws the automatic grace slur (52.05 -> 63.05)
%%abcts                      where ours draws none — `notehead` is undefined for a rest
%%abcts                      and abcjs builds the TieElem anyway.
%%abcts   X:6  [K:G] mid-bar our group is `staff-extra key-signature`; abcjs's is a
%%abcts                      `note` with `selectable="false" data-index="0"`.
%%abcts   X:7  [M:2/4] mid-bar a stem runs 77.51 where abcjs's runs 85.23.
X:1
T:a decoration on a barline, drawn after the barline's own rule
L:1/8
K:C
!fermata!|CDEF|

X:2
T:a tie into a rest, which never closes and runs off the line
L:1/8
K:C
C-z C|

X:3
T:the same tie with no rest, which does close
L:1/8
K:C
C-C C|

X:4
T:a decoration on a rest
L:1/8
K:C
!trill!z4 C4|

X:5
T:a grace group on a rest
L:1/8
K:C
{g}z2 C2|

X:6
T:an inline key change mid-measure
L:1/8
K:C
CD[K:G]EF|

X:7
T:an inline meter change mid-measure
L:1/8
K:C
CD[M:2/4]EF|

X:8
T:a decoration on a barline that opens a measure
L:1/8
K:C
CDEF|!fermata!|GABc|
